        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(slack): bound userCache growth with pruneMapToMaxSize",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`userCache` in Slack monitor context stores resolved user names from `users.info` API calls but has no pruning — every unique user ID accumulates forever. On a busy Slack workspace with thousands of users, this Map grows without bound.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n`channelCache` already uses `pruneMapToMaxSize(channelCache, 1024)` but `userCache` was missed. The fix adds the same pattern at 2048 entries.\n\n## User Impact\n\n- Prevents unbounded memory growth in long-running Slack monitor sessions\n- Oldest entries are evicted when the cap is reached\n- No behavioral change for typical usage (2048 entries covers most workspaces)\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Real Slack API — Token + users.info\n\n```\n$ curl -s -H \"Authorization: Bearer \\$SLACK_TOKEN\" https://slack.com/api/auth.test\n{\n    \"ok\": true,\n    \"bot_id\": \"B0BGACNKEGJ\",\n    \"team_id\": \"T0BG72E2G2Z\",\n    \"user_id\": \"U0BFV1X131V\"\n}\n\n$ curl -s -H \"Authorization: Bearer \\$SLACK_TOKEN\" https://slack.com/api/users.info?user=U0BFV1X131V\n{\n    \"ok\": false,\n    \"error\": \"missing_scope\",\n    \"needed\": \"users:read\",\n    \"provided\": \"channels:history,channels:read,chat:write,...\"\n}\n```\n\nThe token is valid but lacks `users:read` scope, matching the `missing_scope` error path already handled by the catch block in `resolveUserName`. Real Slack workspaces with `users:read` scope would resolve successfully and fill the cache.\n\n### Unit Test — Proves actual eviction\n\n```\n$ node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/slack/src/monitor/context.test.ts\n ✓ evicts the oldest user name when the bounded user cache fills\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  10 passed (10)\n```\n\nTest flow:\n1. resolveUserName(\"U0OLDEST\") → 1 API call, cached\n2. Fill 2048 more users → 2048 API calls, U0OLDEST evicted\n3. Re-request resolveUserName(\"U0OLDEST\") → fresh API call (cache miss)\n4. expect(usersInfo).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(2050) → PASS\n\nWithout eviction, step 3 would return the stale cached entry and total would stay at 2049.\n\n### Lint + Format\n```\n$ npx oxlint -c .oxlintrc.json extensions/slack/src/monitor/context.ts  # No errors\n$ npx oxfmt --check extensions/slack/src/monitor/context.ts              # Correct format\n```\n\n## What Changed\n\n- extensions/slack/src/monitor/context.ts: +2 lines (SLACK_USER_CACHE_MAX_ENTRIES + pruneMapToMaxSize)\n- extensions/slack/src/monitor/context.test.ts: +19 lines (eviction test with re-request assertion)\n\n## AI Assistance 🤖\n- **AI-assisted**: Yes\n- **Co-Authored-By**: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n- **Human confirmed understanding**: Yes",
        "branch": "fix/slack-user-cache-prune",
